() Tj T*
(For \(iv\), verify_reduction.m reconstructs the actual elliptic curve) Tj T*
(and61-point representing P15. Its Tate coordinates have degree15.) Tj T*
(On these coordinates delta_2, delta_3 and delta_4 act as Frobenius to) Tj T*
(the powers2,12 and4, respectively. In particular H15 acts transitively) Tj T*
(on the15 geometric points of P15, so P15 maps to a rational point on) Tj T*
(the special fibre of Z. The weaker assertion \(iv\) suffices below.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All these computations are exact. verify_sage.py independently checks) Tj T*
(the exported rational inclusions, common mod2 kernel, genera and the) Tj T*
(quadric calculation used in Section4. independent_checks.json records) Tj T*
(PASS. This independent linear-algebra check is not a separate agent audit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The curve X has good reduction at2, and H5,H15 have odd order. Their) Tj T*
(tame quotients Y,Z therefore have good reduction at2, with the quotient) Tj T*
(maps and diamond actions extending over Z_2. The map f:X -> Z has) Tj T*
(degree15. Since f_* f^*=[15], its pullback is injective on2-torsion.) Tj T*
(It follows from \(iii\) that J_Z\(Q\)[2]=0 as well.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For an abelian scheme over Z_2, the torsion in the kernel of reduction) Tj T*
(on Q_2-points is killed by2: doubling carries this kernel into the) Tj T*
(modulo4 formal subgroup, on which the formal logarithm is injective.) Tj T*
(Consequently rational torsion reduction is injective on both J_X and) Tj T*
(J_Z. No assertion of injectivity on all rational points is needed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. DESCENT TO AN IRREDUCIBLE CUBIC DIVISOR ON Z) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Suppose such a D exists. Choose a rational cusp c on X, and put) Tj T*
( h=delta_3. Then) Tj T*
( [hD-D]=\(h-1\)[D-15c]+15[hc-c]) Tj T*
(is rational torsion, by \(i\) and Manin--Drinfeld. It reduces to zero,) Tj T*
(by \(iv\). Hence [hD-D]=0. A nonzero principal divisor hD-D would give) Tj T*
(a rational function over Q of degree at most15. This is impossible,) Tj T*
(since gon_Q\(X\)>=325*\(61^2-1\)/65536>15. Thus hD=D as divisors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The order5 group H5 acts freely on characteristic-zero noncuspidal) Tj T*
(points of X: a diamond stabilizer there can only have order dividing) Tj T*
(2 or3, from the extra elliptic automorphisms. Therefore D is the) Tj T*
(pullback of an irreducible cubic divisor D_Y on Y. Its image D_Z on Z) Tj T*
(has degree1 or3. Degree1 would give a rational noncuspidal point on) Tj T*
(X_0\(61\), forbidden by Mazur's rational prime-isogeny theorem. Thus) Tj T*
(D_Z is irreducible of degree3, and f_*D=5D_Z.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reduction commutes with f and the diamonds. Since delta_2 fixes P15,) Tj T*
(we obtain 5*\(s red\(D_Z\)-red\(D_Z\)\)=0 in the divisor group of the special) Tj T*
(fibre of Z. That group is torsion-free, so red\(D_Z\) is s-invariant.) Tj T*
(\(The transitive H15 action above also gives red\(D_Z\)=3S for one) Tj T*
(rational point S.\) Choose a rational cusp c_Z of Z. Then) Tj T*
( [sD_Z-D_Z]=\(s-1\)[D_Z-3c_Z]+3[sc_Z-c_Z]) Tj T*
(is rational torsion by \(ii\) and Manin--Drinfeld on the quotient.) Tj T*
(It reduces to zero, hence [sD_Z-D_Z]=0 by injectivity of torsion) Tj T*
(reduction on J_Z.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
